{
  "$comment": "The big working things of the town's named places (crates/art/outside/src/civic_works, built by cargo art; content/civicWorks.json): the fire engine, fire pole and hose rack, the two-post car lift, tyre rack and tool chest, the printing press, the server rack, the timber stack, cement mixer and flagpole. Listed in the base manifest's packs. The materials map onto the game's finishes so a model costs one draw call per finish group. The fire engine, the car lift and the outdoor things have far versions for the town overview. The press's plate and blanket cylinders turn while a resident watches it run (`rollers`); the server rack's LEDs blink (`blink`) and the flag sways at the top of its pole (`flutter`), both ambient; the server rack's LEDs and its UPS's screen glow at night.",
